, compare Zech 6:8 ; worked by artificer Gen 4:22 (J) 1Kin 7:14 (twice in verse); 2Chr 24:12 ; material — doubtless hardened with alloy, probably tin, making bronze , compare Now Archaeology i. 243 Benz Archaeology 214 — of armour 1Sam 17:5-6 , 1Kin 14:27 , utensils 2Kin 25:14 = Jer 52:18 ; Lev 6:21 ; Num 17:4 + very often, altar 2Kin 16:14-15 , Exod 38:30 ; 39:39 , etc., and other objects Num 21:9 (twice in verse) (JE), 2Kin 18:4 ; 1Kin 4:13 ; 7:15 ff. +, especially in description of tabernacle and temple; cast 7:14 ; polished מְמֹרָט 7:45 , מָרוּק 2Chr 4:16 (compare Lev 6:21 ); and shining מֻצְהָב Ezra 8:27 . On ׳נ קָלָל Ezek 1:7 ; Dan 10:6 see קלל ; ׳נ as spoil of war 2Sam 8:8 ; 2Kin 25:13 = Jer 52:17 , 20 etc. 2 fetters of copper or bronze , usually dual Judg 16:21 ; 2Sam 3:34 ; 2Kin 25:7 = Jer 39:7 ; 52:11 ; 2Chr 36:6 , also 33:11 ; singular only Lam 3:7 (figurative of oppression). 3 as less in value than gold but more than wood Isa 60:17 (twice in verse); figurative of worthless people Jer 6:28 (+ בַּרְזֶל ), id. (as dross of silver) Ezek 22:18 (+ עוֺפֶרֶת בַּרְזֶל, בְּדִיל, ). — On 16:36 see IV. נחשׁ . 4 figurative of pitiless sky Deut 28:23 . II. [ נְח֫שֶׁת ] noun [feminine] suffix נְחֻשְׁתֵּךְ Ezek 16:36 where context (|| עֶרְוָה ) favours meaning lust, harlotry , or specific sens. obscoen. (Co [citing Ki Ra] Berthol, see also Da); text perhaps corrupt (compare Nö ZMG xl (1886). 730 ); Sm proposes תַּזְנוּתַיִךְ , so apparently Toy Hpt ; Or בָּשְׁתֵּךְ .","rootNote":"for 5154 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 15 19","keyReferences":["1Chr 15 19","1Chr 18 8","1Chr 18 8","1Chr 18 8","1Chr 18 10","1Chr 22 3","1Chr 22 14","1Chr 22 16"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":140,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 15 19","book":"1Chr","chapter":15,"verse":19,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"נְחֹ֖שֶׁת","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcfsa"},{"reference":"1Chr 1